一看便知;
3050 因為 RAM 的速度提升了超多;
因而快 RX580 大約10%

 @marianwedingson8235  what are you on bro?? GTX 970 you real rn?
GTX 1080 is one deserving to called aged like fine wine not some goofy aah 970, 
And  RX470 and 580 for amd

 @pietrikoskoskos  Dude, what? The 1070 largely has the rtx 3050's performance and has been out for 6 years. You telling me that, that 1070 will do another 7 years of 1080p gaming? Infact lets be generous and say the rtx 3050 is close to a gtx 1080. You telling the the already 6 year old gtx 1080 will do another 7 years of 1080p gaming? 

Even if you use the dlss argument, dlss will only get better and the future cards will have better dlss implementations. 

Nah. This rtx 3050 will struggle with 1080p gaming. Realistically you'd need rtx 3060 level for 1080p gaming for 5-6 years in the future. The 1060 did 1080p gaming for that long. The rtx 2060 will do so as well. I mean its already 3-4 years old and still does 1080p.

 @Lee_Everett660  The rtx 3050 is not even much faster than the 1070 (5-10fps more at best), despite ampere being out for quite a while now. So what makes you think the 3050 will receive so much optimization when rtx 4000 is just around the corner and will likely blow the rtx 3050 out ofnthe water, if nvidia is rumored to use tsmc's 5nm.

Oh and the rtx 3050 also costs almost as much as the gtx 1070 (~350 vs $380) , uses almost as much power (130w vs 150w). 

Yeah the 1650 super's 4gb vram could be forgiven cause it fucking costed half as much as a rtx 3050. What point you trying to make with 4gb of vram? That you want vram amounts to stay the same? The rtx 3050 better have 8gb of vram now because midrange cards much older than it have had 8gb of vram for quite a while.

 @Lee_Everett660  Oh sure man, not like there's gaming laptops at msrp. 

Or how the rx6600 costs almost as much as the rtx 3050

But sure pal. 3050 is a ''budget'' card even though its ''msrp'' is higher than a 1660s. And in the current market its close to a rx6600 in price

 @jebroz4810  Except, it barely beats a 6 year old midrange card in performance, uses nearly as much power as it, and can cost as much as a rx6600, a card that eats less power and performs better.

Then there's gaming laptops with a rtx 3060. Even a 100w rtx 3060 laptop can be made to be within 10-15% of a desktop rtx 3060. So, around a rx6600. And they can cost $1000ish in the US and around that price in other countries. Given everything they pack, they're good value. 

So yeah. Dlss doesn't justify its shitty price. Or its performance. Or its efficiency.

 @phoenixyt124  I'm sorry mate, but the 1070 ALSO supports FSR. And costing almost nothing? Its street price is basically what the 1070 had costed at launch. 

And hell, if the 3050 is a great 1440p card, so is the 1070. 

I am assuming you've not seen the leaked nvidia rtx 4000 card leak. The next generation of cards are gonna be roughly 2x better. Both AMD and nvidia.

 @setzer-j6s  in our country 3050 is exceptionally cheaper than 1070. Also no one buys RTX for Raytracing. Its almost always for more fps. Or have you seen any YouTuber actually casually play with ray tracing, cause i don’t. 

But i do like your argumentation very much, most people on the internet are really rude to me, but our argument is really peaceful, at least it seems so to me. 

Im convinced you do know about gpus, but i still believe that 3050 will definitely not be useless anytime soon. In my opinion this conversation is over now, we both shared our opinion and it is unclear for now if the 3050 will be useless or not. Apart from that, feel free to comment further, if you want.

 @thatwasawesomedude8883  Oh wow. Except the 1070 is nearly 7 years old. And the 3050 still doesn't really beat a 1660s/ti. 

Also. Moving in to the future, its going to struggle with games. 8Gb is the bare minimum for 1080p now. So lets see how long dlss will keep it alive. 

And lastly, when a so called budget gpu's official MSRP is literally higher than last gen's midrange card, the 1660 super, while not really being any faster and technically using more power, I don't think just 2gb more vram (which is really what it should have) and dlss is gonna make anyone too keen on buying it. Especially when the rx6600 beats the 3050 by 20 to 30%, while using 20 to 30% less power. And it costs the same often times.

 @skorpers   Maybe use context clues to determine the settings I've referenced. 

And getting affordable? To play 1080p you now need a $300 TO $400 gpu and still need a $200 to $250 CPU. Inflation has also reduced the real wages of folks so these prices will still sting. Even games are jacking up in prices and demanding more and more. 

PC gaming is slowly becoming more and more expensive now.

 @invader-zen  Go to my channel and I've overclocked my gtx 1050 to 1924mhz. You can see the performance boost over stock, undervolt and undervolt + overclock. 

So I am sure you can get some performance boost out of overclocking your GTX 1050ti mobile via afterburner. No need to go through vbios or anything. That is only used for raising the power limits. 

Also, the i5 7300hq should use 20-22w under 100% load at its full 3.1ghz boost. Mine does that and remains quite cool. Never hits 80 unless I do something demanding.

 @invader-zen  Actually, the gtx 980m isn't gonna be that much better than a mobile 1050ti. Maybe like 20% better, which isn't much. I mean my legion y520 has just 2 piddly heatpipes shared between the cpu and gpu. Its not very overbuilt. Yet I still keep temps below 70 on gpu when its oc'd to the max. 

I do wish the i5 7300hq allowed a 3.5ghz all core boost. It can clearly handle it without overheating.

Really, you're just better off selling your 1050ti laptop and inspiron for a newer budget rtx 3060 laptop. Or hell even a 4600h + 1650 laptop would obliterate a i7 3720mq and gtx 980m machine. The 4600h alone trades blows with intel's 8 core 10th gen parts. And the gtx 1650 gddr6 when OC'd can match a gtx 970/rx470. I've seen the msi gf65 thin hit $850 and it packs a 144hz panel, 75w rtx 3060 (desktop 2060 level), i5 10500h (when tuned it'll be around a i5 10400f), 8gb ram and a 500gb nvme.

